  "id_note": "Stable identifiers are ASCII slugs of the German lemma; the umlaut/ß spelling lives in \"lemma\".",
  "source_note": "Every lemma below was checked against the official Goethe-Zertifikat A1 (Start Deutsch 1) Wortliste PDF, section 'Alphabetische Wortliste'. The 15 records delivered by PREP-01 keep their ids, fields and order unchanged; TAV-01 (Issue #8) adds 32 further lemmas for the tavern curriculum. This is a candidate A1 list chosen for a tavern shift - it is NOT a frequency ranking and NOT 'the most frequent German words'. No frequency corpus was used.",
  "source_kind_note": "Most entries are printed headwords of the Wortliste and carry source_kind 'headword'. Two entries are not headwords: 'danke' is printed as an indented Nebeneintrag under the headword 'danken', and 'Wie bitte?' is printed as a Redewendung line under the headword 'wie'. Both say so in source_kind and name their parent headword in source_parent, so a reader can tell exactly what the source printed.",
  "gloss_note_extended": "The 32 TAV-01 lemmas are verbs, adjectives, prepositions, an adverb and two everyday expressions, deliberately not nouns: nouns are easy to teach with a clickable prop, and no new prop is committed in this task, so a new noun would be a word the player can read but never point at. Every new lemma therefore carries scene_object null and is introduced in a German sentence instead of as an object.",
  "gloss_note": "English and Russian translations are agent-authored helper glosses and still need human review; the Goethe list itself is monolingual and gives an example sentence instead of a translation. The Russian gloss is what the in-game 'Подсказка · Перевод' button and the end-of-day summary show, so it has to be reviewed by a human before it can be trusted as teaching.",
  "sources": [
    {
